    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, this is a good start. i want to lean more into the physical contrast though. since the empire is very refined and polished, i want the villains to look and feel more... raw. \n\ncan you go deeper into the physical descriptions of the common people in these groups? i want them to look distinctly different from the empire—maybe more rugged or even a bit unkempt to show they don't care about the 'refined' ways of the civilized world. also, what are some of their more 'feral' or instinctual customs that would shock an enlightened citizen of the empire?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, let's delve into the physical details and customs of the Shadows' common folk to emphasize their primal and rugged nature:\n\n**Ironclad Hearts (Common Folk of the Order of Shadows)**  \n- **Appearance**: The common people of the Shadows are built tough, as if they'd likely carved their existence from stones themselves. Their skin is taut and rugged, displaying faint vein patterns as if their veins worked as an extension of their sinews and strength. Their eyes, too, dark and almost glowing, are sharp and vigilant. Long, dirtied hair springs away at the ends, keeping them from tangled in vines or roots.\n- **Culture**: Living in the perilous forest, these people have adapted and thrived in a symbiotic balance with the hexed wildlands. They are skilled trackers and hunters, their lives dictated by the gifts of the forest. They communicate with an ancient, guttural tongue derived from their ancestors’ failures to understand the forest. Food is either foraged, hunted, or grown in patches cleared in the forest.\n- **Scary Traits**: Meddling with arcane energies, harnessing spirits, and invoking the forest's wrath makes them feared and respected invaders of the Empire's enlightened borders.",
      "source": "target",
